  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_010 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is our best result at 0.629 acc / 0.599 F1, clearly outperforming singleprofile (0.535) and transformer aggregation (0.599). However, we have only tested concat fusion and have no evidence about whether weighted fusion can better balance the two modalities. Question: config_002 changes exactly one variable—fusion from concat to weighted—while holding model setting, profile setting, RNA encoder, image encoder, and aggregation identical to config_010. This isolates the effect of the fusion strategy. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a clean single-variable comparison to our current best, directly tests an important and unexplored design axis (how modalities are combined), and the result will inform whether further fusion complexity is warranted or whether budget should shift to exploring alternative encoders (e.g., scvi_n200, scgpt) or image backbones."
}

